Z||000000||Dave85||01-14-2000||09:26 PM||||<BR>Anything I should know before diving in?<BR>Thanks, <BR>Dave<BR>'85 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Dave85 (edited 01-14-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-14-2000||10:20 PM||||If you have a set of instructions you should be good to go.  Everything is straightforward except unscrewing the emergency brake off the piston-it has a one way clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Boxdin||01-15-2000||12:11 AM||||It is vital that the ratchet (or clutch) mechanism inside the piston be functional. I've wasted many hours redoing work because I didn't understand that function||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-15-2000||05:14 PM||||I really don't recomend you rebuild these unless you have the inperson help of someone who does this allot. A regular caliper isn't very dificult and is fairly forgiving of some things. The Fiero rear caliper however has proven to be a problem to rebuild. Very small things will make it not work right or leak.<P>There is a GM rebuild kit that was used for the recall work. If you aren't certain that your calipers are the later ones then this is the kit you want. It includes the parts for both sides. I don't have the number for it, but someone here does. It's been posted before.||||reg||1
